// The colossus's parts (R1; the manual's "Body parts (R1)"): it is hit only through them, never
// through its own 6 m capsule. Meters from its feet in its own frame (forward is where it faces).
//
// - Two legs without health of their own: a hit on a leg takes twice the poise (it topples).
// - A hand resting low in front, reachable with a sword: 60 hp of its own; the body loses half of
//   what the hand takes.
// - A horn on its head, out of a sword's reach: 80 hp.
// - A core in its chest that starts closed (`part ... op=on` opens it): a hit there is tripled and
//   tagged `weak` for a game's damage hooks.
//
// Every part is a lock point (R3, `lock: true`) and the body itself is not (`lock_body: false`): the
// lock-on takes the hand, a leg, the core or the horn, and a swing that overlaps the locked part goes
// through it. A broken part is a lock point no more.
{
    "colossus": (
        body_hurtbox: false,
        lock_body: false,
        parts: {
            "core": (shape: Sphere(radius: 0.6), at: (forward: 0.9, up: 2.0), damage: 3.0, tags: ["weak"], enabled: false, lock: true),
            "hand": (shape: Sphere(radius: 0.5), at: (forward: 1.4, up: 1.2, right: 1.0), health: Some(60), to_body: 0.5, lock: true),
            "horn": (shape: Sphere(radius: 0.5), at: (forward: 0.3, up: 5.7), health: Some(80), lock: true),
            "leg_left": (shape: Capsule(half_height: 0.8, radius: 0.45), at: (forward: 0.3, up: 1.2, right: -0.7), poise: 2.0, lock: true),
            "leg_right": (shape: Capsule(half_height: 0.8, radius: 0.45), at: (forward: 0.3, up: 1.2, right: 0.7), poise: 2.0, lock: true),
        },
    ),
}
